{
  "description": "SiennaGridDB SQL codegen config, consumed by scripts/generate_sql_schema.py. One entry per schema_map.json table. Every property of every mapped component must appear in exactly one of: 'columns' (a column; the value holds overrides), 'attribute_channel' (a row in the generic attributes table), 'decomposed' (split into the DB-only columns it lists), or 'skip' (not stored). A 'columns' entry with 'sql' is a DB-only column with no schema property; its value is the raw declaration after the column name. Column overrides: 'column' (DB name), 'references' (FK target), 'not_null', 'default' (null removes the schema default), 'checks' (extra CHECK expressions), 'comment', and 'unit_base' (base_power_ref / base_voltage_ref for derived pu unit conventions). Table keys: 'comment' (lines above the CREATE TABLE) and 'constraints' (table-level constraints). Columns are emitted in 'columns' order. Rules for choosing a disposition: schema/coverage_decisions.json.",
  "tables": {
    "planning_regions": {
      "columns": {
        "id": {},
        "name": {},
        "description": {"sql": "TEXT NULL"},
        "peak_active_power": {},
        "peak_reactive_power": {},
        "load_response": {},
        "base_power": {"checks": ["base_power > 0"]},
        "power_units": {}
      },
      "comment": [
        "Control or planning areas (PSY Area)."
      ]
